{
  "name": "Class-D Audio Amplifier",
  "description": "A switching audio power amplifier: a triangle-carrier comparator turns the audio input into PWM, a MOSFET half-bridge switches the supply rails, and an LC filter (fc≈21kHz) reconstructs the audio. Run a transient — the 8Ω load recovers a clean sine (voltage gain ≈1.875, ~3.5W, flat 1–8kHz, ~55dB carrier rejection). Note: simplified single-node gate drive (no dead-time), so treat as a teaching/demo stage. (Validated on ngspice.)",
  "tags": [
    "audio",
    "amplifier",
    "class-d",
    "power",
    "pwm",
    "mosfet",
    "advanced"
  ],
